        "text": "Conversations about intelligence frequently provoke strong social reactions. Personally, revealing a very high measured score (I sit within the top 0.001% of the population) has sometimes resulted in misunderstanding and mistreatment. That pattern has made the subject feel isolating: the loneliness stems not from the fact of higher performance but from the negative social dynamics that follow disclosure. I'm fascinated by intelligence as a measurable trait and believe careful testing is a useful tool for self-understanding. My goal with this project is to create a practical, humane theory and set of conversational norms that let people engage with cognitive measurement responsibly — so IQ scores can be treated as data for learning and planning, not as badges or insults.",
