    {
     "original": {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Each letter corresponds to an actionable domain. For each: definition, concrete actions, and measurable proxies.",
      "level": null,
      "number": null,
      "name": "Each letter corresponds to an actionable domain. For each: definition, concrete actions, and measurable proxies."
     },
     "everyone": {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Each letter corresponds to an actionable domain. For each: definition, concrete actions, and measurable proxies.",
      "level": null,
      "number": null,
      "name": "Each letter corresponds to an actionable domain. For each: definition, concrete actions, and measurable proxies."
     }
    },
    {
     "original": {
      "kind": "list",
      "text": "- **Humane (H)**\n  - Definition: Foreground dignity and non-judgment.\n  - Actions: Preface intent; avoid bragging language; normalize opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Dignity cues present in disclosure (binary or 0–1 scale).\n- **Understanding (U)**\n  - Definition: State what the measure captures and its limits.\n  - Actions: Mention test name, administration conditions, percentile, approximate margin of error, and which domains the test targets.\n  - Proxy: Presence/absence of measurement metadata.\n- **Measurement (M)**\n  - Definition: Ensure score provenance and triangulation.\n  - Actions: Prefer professional tests; if using a home or unofficial test, flag it; include corroborating evidence where relevant (work samples, performance records).\n  - Proxy: Test provenance quality score.\n- **Application (A)**\n  - Definition: Link disclosure to constructive next steps.\n  - Actions: Offer a learning plan, request specific collaboration, or state an accommodation need.\n  - Proxy: Presence of an explicit action plan in the conversation.\n- **Nuanced (N)**\n  - Definition: Avoid absolute claims; emphasize conditionality and domain specificity.\n  - Actions: Use qualifying language (\"in this domain,\" \"this suggests,\" \"for me\").\n  - Proxy: Count of qualifying clauses; degree of hedging.\n- **Engagement (E)**\n  - Definition: Structure for two-way, safe dialogue.\n  - Actions: Ask permission to discuss; invite questions; provide opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Presence of engagement invitation and opt-out statement.",
      "level": null,
      "number": null,
      "name": "- **Humane (H)**\n  - Definition: Foreground dignity and non-judgment.\n  - Actions: Preface intent; avoid bragging language; normalize opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Dignity cues present in disclosure (binary or 0–1 scale).\n- **Understanding (U)**\n  - Definition: State what the measure captures and its limits.\n  - Actions: Mention test name, administration conditions, percentile, approximate margin of error, and which domains the test targets.\n  - Proxy: Presence/absence of measurement metadata.\n- **Measurement (M)**\n  - Definition: Ensure score provenance and triangulation.\n  - Actions: Prefer professional tests; if using a home or unofficial test, flag it; include corroborating evidence where relevant (work samples, performance records).\n  - Proxy: Test provenance quality score.\n- **Application (A)**\n  - Definition: Link disclosure to constructive next steps.\n  - Actions: Offer a learning plan, request specific collaboration, or state an accommodation need.\n  - Proxy: Presence of an explicit action plan in the conversation.\n- **Nuanced (N)**\n  - Definition: Avoid absolute claims; emphasize conditionality and domain specificity.\n  - Actions: Use qualifying language (\"in this domain,\" \"this suggests,\" \"for me\").\n  - Proxy: Count of qualifying clauses; degree of hedging.\n- **Engagement (E)**\n  - Definition: Structure for two-way, safe dialogue.\n  - Actions: Ask permission to discuss; invite questions; provide opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Presence of engagement invitation and opt-out statement."
     },
     "everyone": {
      "kind": "list",
      "text": "- **Humane (H)**\n  - Definition: Foreground dignity and non-judgment.\n  - Actions: Preface intent; avoid bragging language; normalize opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Dignity cues present in disclosure (binary or 0–1 scale).\n- **Understanding (U)**\n  - Definition: State what the measure captures and its limits.\n  - Actions: Mention test name, administration conditions, percentile, approximate margin of error, and which domains the test targets.\n  - Proxy: Presence/absence of measurement metadata.\n- **Measurement (M)**\n  - Definition: Ensure score provenance and triangulation.\n  - Actions: Prefer professional tests; if using a home or unofficial test, flag it; include corroborating evidence where relevant (work samples, performance records).\n  - Proxy: Test provenance quality score.\n- **Application (A)**\n  - Definition: Link disclosure to constructive next steps.\n  - Actions: Offer a learning plan, request specific collaboration, or state an accommodation need.\n  - Proxy: Presence of an explicit action plan in the conversation.\n- **Nuanced (N)**\n  - Definition: Avoid absolute claims; emphasize conditionality and domain specificity.\n  - Actions: Use qualifying language (\"in this domain,\" \"this suggests,\" \"for me\").\n  - Proxy: Count of qualifying clauses; degree of hedging.\n- **Engagement (E)**\n  - Definition: Structure for two-way, safe dialogue.\n  - Actions: Ask permission to discuss; invite questions; provide opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Presence of engagement invitation and opt-out statement.",
      "level": null,
      "number": null,
      "name": "- **Humane (H)**\n  - Definition: Foreground dignity and non-judgment.\n  - Actions: Preface intent; avoid bragging language; normalize opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Dignity cues present in disclosure (binary or 0–1 scale).\n- **Understanding (U)**\n  - Definition: State what the measure captures and its limits.\n  - Actions: Mention test name, administration conditions, percentile, approximate margin of error, and which domains the test targets.\n  - Proxy: Presence/absence of measurement metadata.\n- **Measurement (M)**\n  - Definition: Ensure score provenance and triangulation.\n  - Actions: Prefer professional tests; if using a home or unofficial test, flag it; include corroborating evidence where relevant (work samples, performance records).\n  - Proxy: Test provenance quality score.\n- **Application (A)**\n  - Definition: Link disclosure to constructive next steps.\n  - Actions: Offer a learning plan, request specific collaboration, or state an accommodation need.\n  - Proxy: Presence of an explicit action plan in the conversation.\n- **Nuanced (N)**\n  - Definition: Avoid absolute claims; emphasize conditionality and domain specificity.\n  - Actions: Use qualifying language (\"in this domain,\" \"this suggests,\" \"for me\").\n  - Proxy: Count of qualifying clauses; degree of hedging.\n- **Engagement (E)**\n  - Definition: Structure for two-way, safe dialogue.\n  - Actions: Ask permission to discuss; invite questions; provide opt-out.\n  - Proxy: Presence of engagement invitation and opt-out statement."
     }
    }
